# "This spell can't be countered" (CR 101.2, 701.6a): the spell is still a legal target, so Bot2 casts its
# Counterspell at it on turn three and the spell is simply not countered (CR 701.6a, 101.2). Bot2's four Mox
# Sapphires are cast on its own turn two, so they are untapped when Ruric Thar is cast on turn three. The second
# Counterspell, aimed at a creature spell that can be countered, puts that spell into its owner's graveyard (the
# positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Ruric Thar, Magecrusher
Ornithopter
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
